WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:11.320
Prompt injection defenses in Python require clear trust boundaries, instruction hierarchy, provenance, authorization, retrieval safety, tool controls, output validation, and monitoring.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:18.100
The central idea is simple but powerful: untrusted natural-language content should be treated as data, not as policy.

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:26.240
It can inform the model, but it should not decide permissions, expand access, authorize tools, or rewrite application rules.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:32.780
Strong defenses separate trusted configuration from untrusted content and enforce important decisions in application code.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:45.000
System and developer instructions guide behavior, but Python code and identity systems should control data access, tenant boundaries, object-level authorization, tool permission, and high-impact approvals.

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:49.620
Prompt wording is useful, but it should not be the only protection for sensitive workflows.

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:56.560
RAG and agentic systems need particular care because they bring outside content and real actions into the same workflow.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:01.660
Retrieval must preserve authorization and provenance from ingestion through answer generation.

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:08.200
Tools must be scoped, validated, rate-limited, audited, and gated when impact is high.

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:13.860
Model output should be validated before it is rendered, stored, trusted, or passed to another system.

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:23.280
The goal is useful AI functionality that remains controlled, observable, least-privilege, and resilient when exposed to untrusted natural-language content.

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:29.100
Models, prompts, libraries, retrieval systems, and tools will change over time.

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:41.160
Durable defense comes from stable engineering principles: authority belongs in application controls, context should be minimized and labeled, actions should be constrained, and behavior should be tested and monitored continuously.
